<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulick de Burgh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1343</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ulick de Burgh was the founder of the Clanricarde <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-burgh">Burkes</a> of south <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galway">Galway</a>. After the murder of his kinsman William Donn de Burgh, Earl of Ulster, in 1333, he seized the family's lands in southern Connacht and took the Gaelic title Mac William Uachtar, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loughrea">Loughrea</a>. His family adopted Irish law and customs, and his descendants were made earls of Clanricarde in 1543.</p></div>
